WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.750
This is the Transhuman Daily, for Wednesday, November 11.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.550
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in transhumanism.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.580
Prove it.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:20.830
Google DeepMind says its AI agents proved Signal's encryption code really works.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.350
Beam says its one-letter gene edit freed sickl

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.140
e cell patients from severe crises for a year.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.890
Google's Gemini 4 Carbon is out,

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:37.840
with a swarm mode that turns one prompt into a team of agents.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.840
And NVIDIA says its open robot model, GR00T 2,

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.580
can learn new skills from watching people.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.900
But AI agents for errands? In Halloween week,

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.190
they booked just four Uber rides out of millions.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.210
And in a preprint,

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:58.540
a wearable robot thumb let people open a bottle with one hand.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.800
In old mice,

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:06.870
a supplement called vanadyl sulfate cleared worn-out cells and added about 7% to lifespan.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:12.040
And Humacyte's lab-grown blood vessel is starting its first heart bypass trial,

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:13.060
in 10 patients.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.070
In a small Finnish trial,

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:20.520
a vibrating bed plus a blood pressure pill seemed to flush out Alzheimer's-linked proteins.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.420
Closer to home, in a Perth trial,

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:27.570
people on a weight-loss drug who lifted weights got stronger, not weaker.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.120
On to wellbeing. Across 99 long-term studies,

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.490
higher wellbeing was linked to nearly two extra years of life.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.810
And UCSF is launching a study of up to 3,000 real-world psychedelic trips,

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:43.810
good and bad.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.760
Now, the catch. After an OpenAI agent got into a Medicare portal,

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:53.130
Australia will create an AI safety regulator.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:58.630
And the FDA now wants every GLP-1 drug to warn about a rare eye condition.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.660
In robotics,

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:08.250
Ant Group's open-source touch model got a robot hand opening bottles 90% of the time.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:13.250
Meanwhile, a humanoid robot joined an Antarctic ultramarathon.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.130
Its battery gave out after 3 kilometres.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:20.690
Oh, and Columbia engineers made a pillowcase that tracks your heartbeat,

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:22.470
breathing and sleep position.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.340
So, big promises everywhere today. The good news?

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:29.100
More and more of them have to prove it.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.950
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.950
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.040
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.350
Go build the future. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
